Find libiio 1.x headers in their new location too.

libiio 1.0 moved the public headers from %{_includedir}/iio.h to
%{_includedir}/iio/iio.h. The finder's PATH_SUFFIXES only knew the
Homebrew "libiio" layout, so with the system sysroot it looked for
/usr/include/iio.h (gone) and never /usr/include/iio/iio.h, failing
the configure with "missing LibIIO_INCLUDE_DIR" even though the
right libiio was present. Searching the "iio" suffix as well finds
either layout; the include directory then points at the headers and
the in-tree "#include <iio.h>" keeps working unchanged.

--- a/FindLibIIO.cmake
+++ b/FindLibIIO.cmake
@@ -27,7 +27,7 @@
           /opt/local/Library/Frameworks
           ${HOMEBREW_PREFIX}/Cellar/libiio/${PC_LibIIO_VERSION}/Frameworks
           ${HOMEBREW_PREFIX}/Cellar/libiio/${PC_LibIIO_VERSION}
-          PATH_SUFFIXES libiio)
+          PATH_SUFFIXES libiio iio)
 
 find_library(LibIIO_LIBRARY NAMES iio libiio
              HINTS ${PC_LibIIO_LIBDIR} ${PC_LibIIO_LIBRARY_DIRS}
